From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Fri, 6 Nov 2026 00:26:06 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Custody kernel: return_unused; verifier V26: history of lot
 accounts

Kernel (copy of workstreams/10-custody/custody/src/lot.rs, regenerated by
core-kernel.py): return_unused gives goods a use order let out and the
user did not use back to their lot as un-consumed (CONSUMED -= q,
HELD += q, IN_TOTAL unchanged), whole units, within what the lot
consumed, if the lot is usable and has room. A return through the
inbound functions counted the same ore as used and as newly received.
No table changes: RULESET_HASH_V3 and V4 stay as pinned.

Verifier: V26:custody-history compares each Lot account's recorded
states pairwise (post-states in transaction order, then the pinned
slot): identity fixed, IN_TOTAL/OUT_TOTAL/FORFEITED/NONCE never down,
state only forward, an order keeps its terms and never grows, an
expected caravan keeps its quantity; across a close the account is a
new lot. A broken change is a FAIL (CustodyHistoryBroken) at the
transaction that recorded it. Instructions are still not replayed, so
a custody season is never a PASS. tests/custody_history.rs: the
kernel's own histories (18,000 random transitions, return and forfeit
included) never fail; eight forged changes do.

